From: Uke Linux maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: clarify Uke development ABI compilation

Distinguish a compiled EXPERT development interface from runtime firmware
qualification. Keep both defaults n and every admission gate unchanged.
Source only; no build, test or target operation performed.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
@@ -224,9 +224,12 @@
 	help
 	  Build the restricted Uke threshold backend. This is not a firmware
 	  qualification. Every operation also requires a privileged, per-source,
-	  expiring admission lease and matching firmware readback. Leave disabled
-	  until the exact active firmware, reply envelope, threshold semantics,
-	  measurement units and autonomous protection evidence are reviewed.
+	  expiring admission lease and matching firmware readback. The default is
+	  off. An EXPERT development kernel may compile the guarded ABI for
+	  admission testing; compilation does not qualify firmware or permit an
+	  operation without reviewed per-boot runtime admission. Exact active
+	  firmware, reply envelope, threshold semantics, measurement units and
+	  autonomous protection evidence must be reviewed before operations.
 	  No PD, current, voltage, factory or gauge control is enabled here.
 
 config BATTERY_QCOM_BATTMGR_UKE_CURRENT
@@ -235,8 +238,10 @@
 	default n
 	help
 	  Build the separately admitted positive constant-current backend for
-	  exact Uke OEM wire property 12. Per-boot evidence must establish its
-	  units, readback, effective behavior and firmware-owned CV/protections.
+	  exact Uke OEM wire property 12. Development compilation alone permits
+	  no operation and leaves runtime qualification off. Per-boot evidence
+	  must establish its units, readback, effective behavior and firmware-owned
+	  CV/protections.
 	  This does not enable the ambiguous thermal-level property 10, voltage
 	  writes, raw properties, PD negotiation or negative/reset sentinels.
 
